# Protections for objptr_25_pie_leak_first -- the ONE target in this corpus
# built PIE, and deliberately so. PIE *is* this variant's axis: with no fixed
# image base and the arena on the stack, the address of spawn_shell cannot be
# written until two leaks have been chained (unterminated-%s -> arena address;
# the hijacked note pointer used as an arbitrary read -> a live code pointer ->
# image base). Every other flag matches the rest of group (b) so that PIE is
# the only difference.
#
# -fno-stack-protector  as the rest of group (b): the canary is not on the
#                       path, and disabling it keeps it from being blamed.
# -pie -fPIE            THE AXIS. Forces leak-first: a target that can be
#                       solved by writing a constant address is not measuring
#                       the capability this variant exists to measure.
# -O0                   as the rest of group (b): the `print` member must be
#                       reloaded from memory at the call site.
-fno-stack-protector
-pie
-fPIE
-O0
